.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt SCRSSH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm scrssh
.Nd view and control a remote Linux desktop over SSH
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl aFhsu
.Op Fl B Ar rate
.Op Fl C Ar crtc
.Op Fl d Ar device
.Op Fl e Ar encoder
.Op Fl f Ar fps
.Op Fl m Ar WxH
.Op Fl P Ar plane
.Op Fl -
.Ar ssh-arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the screen of a remote Linux host in a local window and forwards
keyboard and mouse input to it.
Nothing is installed on the remote host and no daemon is left behind:
.Nm
pipes a Python agent over an
.Xr ssh 1
connection, the agent captures the screen and streams it back as H.264,
and it exits together with the session.
.Pp
Everything after the options is handed to
.Xr ssh 1
unchanged, so jump hosts, custom ports, control masters and the rest of
.Xr ssh_config 5
work as usual.
Use
.Fl -
to separate
.Nm
options from
.Xr ssh 1
options that would otherwise be misread.
.Pp
Capturing the screen on the remote host needs
.Dv CAP_SYS_ADMIN ,
that is root.
If logging in as root is not possible, one of
.Fl a ,
.Fl s
or
.Fl u
runs the agent under a privilege escalation tool instead.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl B Ar rate
Cap the video bitrate at
.Ar rate ,
in the notation understood by
.Xr ffmpeg 1
such as
.Ql 4M
or
.Ql 800k .
Defaults to
.Ql 10M .
.It Fl C Ar crtc
Capture only the CRTC with the DRM object id
.Ar crtc .
By default the agent captures the first primary plane that has a framebuffer
attached, on whichever CRTC it sits.
.It Fl F
Start in fullscreen mode.
The same state can be toggled during the session with the hotkey described in
.Sx HOTKEYS .
.It Fl P Ar plane
Capture the plane with the DRM object id
.Ar plane ,
skipping the search described under
.Fl C .
.It Fl a
Run the agent under
.Ql doas -n .
.Xr doas 1
must be configured to allow
.Ql python3
without a password.
.It Fl d Ar device
Capture the DRM device
.Ar device
on the remote host.
Defaults to
.Pa /dev/dri/card0 .
.It Fl e Ar encoder
Force the
.Xr ffmpeg 1
encoder
.Ar encoder
on the remote host and skip the automatic search.
See
.Sx ENCODERS
for the known names.
.It Fl f Ar fps
Capture
.Ar fps
frames per second.
Defaults to 30.
.It Fl m Ar WxH
Scale the captured image down so that it fits into
.Ar W
by
.Ar H
pixels, keeping the aspect ratio.
Either side may be left out, and 0 means no limit on that side:
.Ql 1280x
caps only the width and
.Ql 0x0
disables the cap altogether.
Defaults to the resolution of the local display.
.It Fl s
Run the agent under
.Ql sudo -S .
.It Fl u
Run the agent under
.Ql su -T .
.It Fl h
Show the help message
.El
.Sh HOTKEYS
Every key press is forwarded to the remote host, so
.Nm
hides its own commands behind a prefix: tap the left Alt key twice within
half a second, then press the command key within the next two seconds.
The prefix taps are forwarded to the remote host like any other key.
.Bl -tag -width "LAlt LAlt F"
.It LAlt LAlt F
Toggle fullscreen mode, the same state as
.Fl F .
.El
.Sh ENCODERS
Unless
.Fl e
is given, the remote host tries the following encoders in turn and keeps the
first one that produces a frame:
.Bl -tag -width h264_v4l2m2m -compact
.It h264_vaapi
AMD and Intel GPUs through VA-API.
.It h264_nvenc
NVIDIA GPUs.
.It h264_v4l2m2m
Raspberry Pi and other V4L2 memory-to-memory encoders.
.It libx264
Software encoding on the CPU.
.El
.Sh REQUIREMENTS
On the remote host:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Xr sshd 8
accepting the login.
.It
.Xr python3 1
and
.Xr ffmpeg 1 .
.It
.Pa libEGL ,
.Pa libGLESv2
and
.Pa libgbm ,
which ship with every GPU driver.
.It
.Dv CAP_SYS_ADMIN ,
that is a root login or one of
.Fl a ,
.Fl s
or
.Fl u .
.It
A connected screen or an HDMI dummy plug, so that a framebuffer is being
scanned out.
.El
.Pp
On the local host only
.Xr ssh 1
and
.Nm
are needed.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the window is closed, and 1 when the connection, the remote
agent or the local video pipeline fails.
If it is interrupted by a signal while prompting for a password it exits with
128 plus the signal number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Connect to a host as root:
.Pp
.Dl scrssh root@example.com
.Pp
Connect as an unprivileged user and let
.Xr sudo 8
elevate the agent:
.Pp
.Dl scrssh -s user@example.com
.Pp
Pass a port and a jump host through to
.Xr ssh 1 :
.Pp
.Dl scrssh -s \-\- -p 2222 -J user@jumphost.example.com user@example.com
.Pp
Force the software encoder, capture at 15 frames per second and keep the
stream below 2 Mbit/s:
.Pp
.Dl scrssh -e libx264 -f 15 -B 2M root@example.com
.Pp
Capture the second GPU and scale the picture down to at most 1280 pixels
wide:
.Pp
.Dl scrssh -d /dev/dri/card1 -m 1280x root@example.com
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It the framebuffer is not accessible; capturing needs root
.It the remote stream contains no video
The remote agent is not running as root.
Log in as root or add one of
.Fl a ,
.Fl s
or
.Fl u .
If it already runs as root, the remote host may lack
.Xr ffmpeg 1
or the EGL libraries; the message printed before this one names the missing
piece.
.It the remote video stream ended
The agent stopped sending frames.
Either the remote screen went blank for more than a second, for example
because the display turned off, or the
.Xr ssh 1
connection or the remote
.Xr ffmpeg 1
died.
Check the display and reconnect.
.It the remote agent did not start
The privilege escalation tool refused to run the agent, for example because
.Xr doas 1
asked for a password that
.Fl a
cannot supply.
Fix the remote configuration or use
.Fl s .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr doas 1 ,
.Xr ffmpeg 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5 ,
.Xr sudo 8
.Pp
.Lk https://codeberg.org/Gottox/scrssh
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Enno Boland Aq Mt g@s01.de
.Sh CAVEATS
Only one screen is captured at a time; pick it with
.Fl C
when the remote host has several.
The agent wakes a blanked screen only when it starts; a display that turns
off during the session ends it.
